                  </origin>
                  <provenance type="#e" source="3217"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_257">Higham Ferrers,
                        Northamptonshire. College of St Mary the Virgin, St Thomas the Martyr and St
                        Edward the Confessor</orgName><p>For the inscr. see under All Souls
                        College, Oxford: the name of Higham Ferrers College has been erased and that
                        of All Souls College, Oxford, q. v., substituted, probably in s. xvi: the
                        words "animarum omnium ... oxon." are on erasure of a Higham Ferrers inscr.,
                        probably "b[eate marie sancti] th[ome Cantuariensis et sancti e]d[war]d[i
                        con]fessoris de [higham ferrer]s". Letters in brackets are illegible by
                        ordinary light.</p></provenance>
               <provenance type="#e" source="4279"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_425">Oxford, Oxfordshire.
                        All Souls' College</orgName><p>'Memorandum quod anno Domini millesimo cccc
                        uicesimo octauo reverendissimus in Christo pater et dominus dominus Henricus
                        Dei gratia Cantuar. archiep. [sc. Henricus Chichele] donauit istum librum
                        Euangeliorum collegio suo Animarum omnium fidelium defunctorum in
                        universitate Oxon' Lincolnien. dioc'' (fol. 8r), and anathema. The words
                        'Animarum ... Oxon.' are on erasure and of s. xvi (?); and All Souls as not
                        founded until 1437--1438; given to Higham Ferrers (founded 1422, q.
                     v.).</p></provenance>
               </history>
